/* B2 · topics 1–5 (format: see a2-part1.js). */
module.exports = [
  { title: 'Global issues', lessons: [
    { t: ['Poverty and inequality', 'Qashshoqlik va tengsizlik'],
      obj: ['Qashshoqlik va tengsizlikning sabab-oqibatlarini muhokama qilasiz.', 'You will discuss the causes and effects of poverty and inequality.'],
      ex: ['Mavzu so‘zlari: poverty line (qashshoqlik chegarasi), gap between rich and poor, income, unemployment, access to (… ga kirish imkoni), basic needs. Sabab: result from, be caused by, stem from (… dan kelib chiqmoq); oqibat: lead to, give rise to, contribute to.\nMurakkab tuzilma: The widening gap between the rich and the poor is largely due to unequal access to education. Inversiya: Not only does poverty harm health, but it also limits education. Aniq ko‘rsatkich: Nearly a tenth of the world’s population lives on less than two dollars a day.', 'Topic words: poverty line, gap between rich and poor, income, unemployment, access to, basic needs. Cause: result from, be caused by, stem from; effect: lead to, give rise to, contribute to.\nComplex structures: The widening gap between the rich and the poor is largely due to unequal access to education. Inversion: Not only does poverty harm health, but it also limits education. Evidence: Nearly a tenth of the world’s population lives on less than two dollars a day.'],
      eg: [['Poverty often stems from a lack of education.', 'Qashshoqlik ko‘pincha ta’limning yetishmasligidan kelib chiqadi.'], ['Unequal access to schools contributes to the gap between rich and poor.', 'Maktablarga teng bo‘lmagan kirish boylar va kambag‘allar o‘rtasidagi tafovutga hissa qo‘shadi.'], ['Not only does poverty harm health, but it also limits opportunities.', 'Qashshoqlik sog‘liqqa zarar yetkazibgina qolmay, imkoniyatlarni ham cheklaydi.'], ['Governments should invest in basic services.', 'Hukumatlar asosiy xizmatlarga sarmoya kiritishi kerak.']],
      w: [['poverty', 'qashshoqlik', 'бедность', 'noun', 'Poverty affects millions of children.', 'Qashshoqlik millionlab bolalarga ta’sir qiladi.', 'ˈpɒvəti'], ['inequality', 'tengsizlik', 'неравенство', 'noun', 'Income inequality is growing.', 'Daromad tengsizligi o‘smoqda.', 'ˌɪnɪˈkwɒləti'], ['unemployment', 'ishsizlik', 'безработица', 'noun', 'Unemployment is high among young people.', 'Yoshlar orasida ishsizlik yuqori.', 'ˌʌnɪmˈplɔɪmənt'], ['stem from', 'kelib chiqmoq', 'проистекать', 'phrasal verb', 'Problems stem from poor planning.', 'Muammolar yomon rejalashtirishdan kelib chiqadi.', 'stem frɒm'], ['widen', 'kengaymoq', 'расширяться', 'verb', 'The gap continues to widen.', 'Tafovut kengayishda davom etmoqda.', 'ˈwaɪdn'], ['deprived', 'mahrum bo‘lgan', 'обездоленный', 'adjective', 'Deprived communities need help.', 'Mahrum jamoalarga yordam kerak.', 'dɪˈpraɪvd']],
      g: [['Not only ___ poverty harm health, but it also limits education.', 'does', 'is', 'has', 'Inversiya: Not only does + subyekt.'], ['The gap between rich and poor is largely ___ to unequal access to education.', 'due', 'owing from', 'cause', '“due to” — … tufayli.']],
      dlg: ['Presenter: Today we discuss inequality. Dr Karimov, what is its main cause? Dr Karimov: It largely stems from unequal access to quality education. Presenter: And the effects? Dr Karimov: Not only does it limit individual opportunities, but it also slows economic growth. Presenter: What should governments do? Dr Karimov: Invest in schools and health care in deprived regions.', 'According to Dr Karimov, where should governments invest?', 'In schools and health care in deprived regions', 'In the army', 'In luxury housing', 'He says “Invest in schools and health care in deprived regions”.'],
      rd: ['Despite global economic growth, the gap between the richest and the poorest continues to widen. Economists argue that inequality is not only a moral problem; it also reduces social mobility and weakens economic stability. Children from deprived families often leave school early, which limits their future earnings and passes poverty from one generation to the next. Some countries have reduced the gap through progressive taxes and free education, while others have seen it grow as a result of unemployment and rising prices.', ['What passes poverty from one generation to the next?', 'Leaving school early and low earnings', 'High taxes', 'Free education'], ['Inequality has fallen worldwide.', 'False'], ['Progressive taxes were introduced in the 18th century.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write 10 sentences on the causes and effects of poverty in the modern world and one realistic solution.', 'stem from|lead to|not only|should', 70, 'Poverty remains one of the most serious problems of our time. It often stems from unemployment and a lack of education. As a result, families cannot afford basic needs. Not only does poverty harm health, but it also limits future opportunities. To tackle the problem, governments should invest in schools and create jobs. International cooperation can also contribute to progress.'],
      sp: ['Explain, in one minute, why the gap between rich and poor is growing and what could be done.', 'The gap is growing because of unequal access to education. Governments should invest in schools and create jobs.'],
      ts: [['Words that mean “result from”:', 'stem from', 'lead to', 'give up'], ['“Tengsizlik” in English:', 'inequality', 'unemployment', 'poverty'], ['The gap continues to ___.', 'widen', 'wide', 'wideness']] },
    { t: ['Globalisation', 'Globallashuv'],
      obj: ['Globallashuvning afzallik va xavflarini muvozanatli baholaysiz.', 'You will weigh up the benefits and risks of globalisation.'],
      ex: ['Globallashuv: free trade, multinational company, outsourcing, import / export, cultural exchange, local industries, competitive. Qiyosiy bog‘lovchilar: While / Whereas / Although (qarama-qarshilik), Consequently / As a consequence (natija), Nevertheless (shunday bo‘lsa-da).\nHedging (ehtiyotkor ifoda): Globalisation tends to benefit large companies. It may lead to job losses. It could be argued that… — mutlaq da’vodan qochish. Majhul: Goods are traded across the world.', 'Globalisation: free trade, multinational company, outsourcing, import / export, cultural exchange, local industries, competitive. Contrast linkers: While / Whereas / Although; result: Consequently / As a consequence; Nevertheless.\nHedging: Globalisation tends to benefit large companies. It may lead to job losses. It could be argued that… avoid absolute claims. Passive: Goods are traded across the world.'],
      eg: [['Globalisation tends to benefit large companies.', 'Globallashuv yirik kompaniyalarga foyda keltirishga moyil.'], ['While trade creates jobs, it may destroy local industries.', 'Savdo ish o‘rinlari yaratsa-da, mahalliy sanoatni yo‘q qilishi mumkin.'], ['Consequently, small businesses struggle to compete.', 'Natijada kichik bizneslar raqobatlashishga qiynaladi.'], ['It could be argued that cultural exchange enriches societies.', 'Madaniy almashinuv jamiyatlarni boyitadi, deyish mumkin.']],
      w: [['globalisation', 'globallashuv', 'глобализация', 'noun', 'Globalisation has changed trade.', 'Globallashuv savdoni o‘zgartirdi.', 'ˌɡləʊbəlaɪˈzeɪʃn'], ['outsource', 'ishni tashqariga topshirmoq', 'передавать на аутсорсинг', 'verb', 'Companies outsource customer service.', 'Kompaniyalar mijozlarga xizmatni tashqariga beradi.', 'ˈaʊtsɔːs'], ['multinational', 'ko‘p millatli', 'международная', 'adjective', 'A multinational company hires thousands.', 'Ko‘p millatli kompaniya minglab odam yollaydi.', 'ˌmʌltiˈnæʃnəl'], ['export', 'eksport qilmoq', 'экспортировать', 'verb', 'We export cotton.', 'Biz paxta eksport qilamiz.', 'ɪkˈspɔːt'], ['consequently', 'natijada', 'следовательно', 'adverb', 'Consequently, prices rose.', 'Natijada narxlar oshdi.', 'ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli'], ['competitive', 'raqobatbardosh', 'конкурентоспособный', 'adjective', 'The market is highly competitive.', 'Bozor juda raqobatli.', 'kəmˈpetətɪv']],
      g: [['___ trade creates jobs, it may destroy local industries.', 'While', 'Despite', 'Therefore', '“While” — qarama-qarshilik bog‘lovchisi.'], ['Globalisation ___ to benefit large companies.', 'tends', 'tend', 'tending', 'Hedging: tends to.']],
      dlg: ['Interviewer: Is globalisation good for developing countries? Economist: It could be argued that it brings investment and jobs. Interviewer: And the downsides? Economist: Local industries may struggle to compete with multinational companies. Consequently, governments need to support small businesses.', 'What do governments need to do?', 'Support small businesses', 'Close their borders', 'Stop exporting', 'The economist says “support small businesses”.'],
      rd: ['Few developments have shaped the modern world as much as globalisation. Falling transport costs and the internet allow companies to produce goods in one country, sell them in another and outsource services to a third. Consumers benefit from lower prices and wider choice. However, critics point out that workers in richer countries may lose jobs, while workers in poorer countries sometimes face low wages. Cultural traditions can also be weakened as global brands spread. Most economists agree that the key is not to reject globalisation, but to manage it fairly.', ['What do most economists agree on?', 'Globalisation should be managed fairly', 'Globalisation should be stopped', 'Wages are equal worldwide'], ['Consumers lose from globalisation.', 'False'], ['The internet was invented in 1969.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a balanced paragraph (10–12 sentences) on the advantages and disadvantages of globalisation; use hedging and contrast linkers.', 'while|consequently|tends to|it could be argued', 70, 'Globalisation has both benefits and drawbacks. On the one hand, it tends to lower prices and widen choice for consumers. While multinational companies create jobs, they may also push small local firms out of business. Consequently, some communities lose their traditional industries. It could be argued that cultural exchange is a benefit, but it may weaken local traditions. Overall, governments should manage globalisation carefully.'],
      sp: ['Give one advantage and one disadvantage of globalisation, using hedging.', 'Globalisation tends to lower prices. However, it may harm small local businesses.'],
      ts: [['Giving work to another company abroad:', 'outsource', 'export', 'widen'], ['“Natijada” in English:', 'consequently', 'whereas', 'despite'], ['Prices ___ to fall with free trade.', 'tend', 'tends to be', 'tending']] },
    { t: ['Migration', 'Migratsiya'],
      obj: ['Migratsiya sabablari, afzalliklari va muammolarini tahlil qilasiz.', 'You will analyse the causes, benefits and challenges of migration.'],
      ex: ['Migratsiya: immigrant / emigrant, refugee (qochoqlar), asylum (boshpana), integrate (singishmoq), brain drain (aqllar ketishi), remittances (pul o‘tkazmalari), push and pull factors. Sabablar: push factors — urush, ishsizlik; pull factors — yaxshi maosh, xavfsizlik.\nParticiple clauses: Fleeing from war, many families leave their homes. (= Because they flee…) Having arrived in a new country, they face language barriers. Raqamlar bilan: roughly, approximately, about one in thirty people.', 'Migration: immigrant / emigrant, refugee, asylum, integrate, brain drain, remittances, push and pull factors. Causes: push factors — war, unemployment; pull factors — better pay, safety.\nParticiple clauses: Fleeing from war, many families leave their homes. Having arrived in a new country, they face language barriers. Numbers: roughly, approximately, about one in thirty people.'],
      eg: [['Fleeing from war, many families leave their homes.', 'Urushdan qochib, ko‘p oilalar uylarini tark etadi.'], ['Having arrived in a new country, they face language barriers.', 'Yangi mamlakatga kelgach, ular til to‘siqlariga duch keladi.'], ['Remittances support millions of families.', 'Pul o‘tkazmalari millionlab oilalarni qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi.'], ['Roughly one in thirty people lives abroad.', 'Taxminan har o‘ttiz kishidan biri chet elda yashaydi.']],
      w: [['immigrant', 'muhojir (kirib kelgan)', 'иммигрант', 'noun', 'Many immigrants work in construction.', 'Ko‘p muhojirlar qurilishda ishlaydi.', 'ˈɪmɪɡrənt'], ['refugee', 'qochoq', 'беженец', 'noun', 'Refugees need shelter.', 'Qochoqlarga boshpana kerak.', 'ˌrefjuˈdʒiː'], ['integrate', 'singishmoq', 'интегрироваться', 'verb', 'It takes time to integrate.', 'Singishib ketish vaqt oladi.', 'ˈɪntɪɡreɪt'], ['remittance', 'pul o‘tkazmasi', 'денежный перевод', 'noun', 'Remittances help rural families.', 'Pul o‘tkazmalari qishloq oilalariga yordam beradi.', 'rɪˈmɪtns'], ['brain drain', 'aqllar ketishi', 'утечка мозгов', 'noun', 'Brain drain harms small countries.', 'Aqllar ketishi kichik davlatlarga zarar.', 'breɪn dreɪn'], ['asylum', 'boshpana (siyosiy)', 'убежище', 'noun', 'He applied for asylum.', 'U siyosiy boshpana so‘radi.', 'əˈsaɪləm']],
      g: [['___ from war, many families leave their homes.', 'Fleeing', 'Fled', 'To flee', 'Participle clause (-ing): ular qochayotganda.'], ['___ arrived in a new country, they face language barriers.', 'Having', 'Have', 'Had', 'Perfect participle: Having + V3.']],
      dlg: ['Reporter: Why do people emigrate? Researcher: There are push factors, such as unemployment, and pull factors, such as better wages. Reporter: What about the receiving country? Researcher: Having integrated, immigrants usually fill labour gaps and pay taxes. Reporter: And the home country? Researcher: It loses skilled workers, but receives remittances.', 'What does the home country receive?', 'Remittances', 'More taxes', 'More refugees', 'The researcher says “receives remittances”.'],
      rd: ['Around 280 million people live outside the country where they were born. Some leave voluntarily, attracted by higher salaries or educational opportunities; others, forced by conflict or natural disasters, become refugees. Receiving countries often benefit from migrants’ skills and energy, yet integration can be difficult because of language barriers and discrimination. Countries of origin face a dilemma: they lose talented workers, a phenomenon called brain drain, but they also receive remittances that support families and local economies.', ['What is “brain drain”?', 'Loss of skilled workers', 'A health problem', 'A kind of tax'], ['All migrants leave voluntarily.', 'False'], ['Most migrants go to Canada.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write an essay paragraph (10 sentences) explaining push and pull factors of migration and one effect on the home country.', 'push|pull|having|as a result', 70, 'People migrate for many reasons. Push factors, such as war and unemployment, force people to leave. Pull factors, such as better wages, attract them abroad. Having arrived, migrants often face language barriers. As a result, integration takes time. The home country may suffer brain drain, but it also receives remittances.'],
      sp: ['Explain push and pull factors in your own words.', 'Push factors are problems at home, like unemployment. Pull factors are attractions abroad, like better pay.'],
      ts: [['A person forced to leave because of war:', 'refugee', 'remittance', 'asylum'], ['“Singishmoq” in English:', 'integrate', 'outsource', 'widen'], ['___ finished school, he emigrated.', 'Having', 'Be', 'Had to']] },
    { t: ['Discussing global problems', 'Global muammolarni muhokama qilish'],
      obj: ['Global muammolar bo‘yicha munozarada fikr bildirasiz, rozi bo‘lasiz va e’tiroz bildirasiz.', 'You will give opinions, agree and disagree in a discussion on global problems.'],
      ex: ['Munozara iboralari: Fikr: From my point of view…, I’m convinced that… Rozilik: I couldn’t agree more. That’s exactly what I think. Qisman: I partly agree, but… E’tiroz: I see your point, but I’m not sure that… I’m afraid I disagree. To‘xtatish: May I just add…? Aniqlashtirish: What exactly do you mean by…?\nGlobal mavzular: climate change, poverty, pandemics, conflict, water shortage. Yechim: tackle (hal qilishga kirishmoq), address, combat, raise awareness, international cooperation.', 'Discussion language: Opinion: From my point of view…, I’m convinced that… Agreeing: I couldn’t agree more. That’s exactly what I think. Partly: I partly agree, but… Disagreeing: I see your point, but I’m not sure that… I’m afraid I disagree. Interrupting: May I just add…? Clarifying: What exactly do you mean by…?\nGlobal topics: climate change, poverty, pandemics, conflict, water shortage. Solutions: tackle, address, combat, raise awareness, international cooperation.'],
      eg: [['I couldn’t agree more.', 'Men to‘liq qo‘shilaman.'], ['I see your point, but I’m not sure that it’s realistic.', 'Fikringizni tushundim, lekin bu realistik ekaniga ishonchim komil emas.'], ['We must tackle climate change together.', 'Biz iqlim o‘zgarishini birgalikda hal qilishimiz kerak.'], ['What exactly do you mean by “sustainable”?', '“Sustainable” deganda aynan nimani nazarda tutyapsiz?']],
      w: [['tackle', 'hal qilishga kirishmoq', 'решать', 'verb', 'We must tackle the problem now.', 'Biz muammoni hozir hal qilishga kirishishimiz kerak.', 'ˈtækl'], ['combat', 'kurashmoq', 'бороться', 'verb', 'Vaccines help combat disease.', 'Vaksinalar kasallikka qarshi kurashishga yordam beradi.', 'ˈkɒmbæt'], ['awareness', 'xabardorlik', 'осведомлённость', 'noun', 'We need to raise awareness.', 'Xabardorlikni oshirish kerak.', 'əˈweənəs'], ['cooperation', 'hamkorlik', 'сотрудничество', 'noun', 'International cooperation is essential.', 'Xalqaro hamkorlik zarur.', 'kəʊˌɒpəˈreɪʃn'], ['convinced', 'ishongan', 'убеждённый', 'adjective', 'I am convinced that he is right.', 'Uning haqligiga ishonaman.', 'kənˈvɪnst'], ['realistic', 'real, amaliy', 'реалистичный', 'adjective', 'This plan is realistic.', 'Bu reja amaliy.', 'ˌriːəˈlɪstɪk']],
      g: [['I couldn’t ___ more.', 'agree', 'agreeing', 'to agree', 'Qat’iy rozilik iborasi.'], ['We must ___ climate change together.', 'tackle', 'tackling', 'to tackling', 'must + asosiy fe’l.']],
      dlg: ['Moderator: Can global problems be solved by one country? Ali: From my point of view, no. International cooperation is essential. Dilnoza: I couldn’t agree more, but is it realistic? Ali: I see your point, but we have done it before with the ozone layer. Dilnoza: That’s a fair example. May I just add that awareness also matters?', 'What example does Ali use?', 'The ozone layer', 'The internet', 'Space travel', 'Ali says “the ozone layer”.'],
      rd: ['In a recent debate, students discussed whether young people can influence global problems. Those in favour argued that social media raises awareness quickly and that young voters can change policies. The opposing side claimed that individual action is too small to matter without government support. In the end, both sides agreed that cooperation between citizens, companies and governments is the most effective way to combat problems such as climate change and poverty.', ['What did both sides agree on?', 'Cooperation is the most effective way', 'Young people have no influence', 'Social media is harmful'], ['The students refused to discuss the topic.', 'False'], ['The debate lasted three hours.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a short dialogue (12 lines) of a discussion about a global problem, with agreeing and disagreeing expressions.', 'from my point of view|i couldn’t agree more|i see your point|however', 70, 'A: From my point of view, climate change is the biggest problem. B: I couldn’t agree more. A: We need international cooperation. B: I see your point, but is it realistic? A: Yes, if governments act together. B: May I add that raising awareness also helps? A: Of course.'],
      sp: ['Give your opinion on a global problem and respond to an opposing view.', 'From my point of view, climate change is the biggest problem. I see your point about poverty, but I’m not sure it is more urgent.'],
      ts: [['Strong agreement:', 'I couldn’t agree more.', 'I’m afraid I disagree.', 'What do you mean?'], ['“Xabardorlik” in English:', 'awareness', 'cooperation', 'combat'], ['Let’s ___ the problem together.', 'tackle', 'tackles', 'tackling to']] },
  ], exam: [['___ finished the course, she found a job abroad.', 'Having', 'Be', 'Had', 'grammar'], ['Companies often ___ customer service to other countries.', 'outsource', 'integrate', 'widen', 'vocabulary'], ['Poverty ___ from a lack of education.', 'stems', 'steams', 'stay', 'grammar']] },

  { title: 'Technology and society', lessons: [
    { t: ['Artificial intelligence and automation', 'Sun’iy intellekt va avtomatlashtirish'],
      obj: ['Sun’iy intellekt va avtomatlashtirishning jamiyatga ta’sirini muhokama qilasiz.', 'You will discuss the impact of artificial intelligence and automation on society.'],
      ex: ['Sun’iy intellekt: algorithm, machine learning, automation, robot, data, replace human workers, creative tasks, bias (xolislik yo‘qligi). Kelajak: Will vs be going to; Future Perfect: By 2040, many routine jobs will have been automated. Future Continuous: In ten years, we will be working alongside robots.\nHedging: It is widely believed that…, Experts predict that…, It is likely/unlikely that… Natija: This will result in…, which in turn…',  'AI: algorithm, machine learning, automation, robot, data, replace human workers, creative tasks, bias. Future: Future Perfect: By 2040, many routine jobs will have been automated. Future Continuous: In ten years, we will be working alongside robots.\nHedging: It is widely believed that…, Experts predict that…, It is likely/unlikely that… Consequence: This will result in…, which in turn…'],
      eg: [['By 2040, many routine jobs will have been automated.', '2040-yilga kelib ko‘p oddiy ishlar avtomatlashtirilgan bo‘ladi.'], ['In ten years, we will be working alongside robots.', 'O‘n yildan keyin biz robotlar bilan yonma-yon ishlayotgan bo‘lamiz.'], ['Algorithms can reflect the bias in their data.', 'Algoritmlar o‘z ma’lumotlaridagi xolislik yo‘qligini aks ettirishi mumkin.'], ['It is widely believed that creativity cannot be automated.', 'Ijodkorlikni avtomatlashtirib bo‘lmaydi, deb keng hisoblanadi.']],
      w: [['algorithm', 'algoritm', 'алгоритм', 'noun', 'The algorithm recommends videos.', 'Algoritm videolarni tavsiya qiladi.', 'ˈælɡərɪðəm'], ['automation', 'avtomatlashtirish', 'автоматизация', 'noun', 'Automation changes the job market.', 'Avtomatlashtirish mehnat bozorini o‘zgartiradi.', 'ˌɔːtəˈmeɪʃn'], ['machine learning', 'mashinali o‘rganish', 'машинное обучение', 'noun', 'Machine learning needs data.', 'Mashinali o‘rganish ma’lumot talab qiladi.', 'məˈʃiːn ˈlɜːnɪŋ'], ['bias', 'xolislik yo‘qligi', 'предвзятость', 'noun', 'The system showed bias.', 'Tizimda xolislik yo‘qligi ko‘rindi.', 'ˈbaɪəs'], ['replace', 'o‘rnini bosmoq', 'заменять', 'verb', 'Robots may replace drivers.', 'Robotlar haydovchilar o‘rnini bosishi mumkin.', 'rɪˈpleɪs'], ['routine', 'doimiy, odatiy', 'рутинный', 'adjective', 'Routine tasks are easy to automate.', 'Odatiy vazifalarni avtomatlashtirish oson.', 'ruːˈtiːn']],
      g: [['By 2040, many jobs ___ automated.', 'will have been', 'will be being', 'have', 'Future Perfect Passive.'], ['In ten years we ___ alongside robots.', 'will be working', 'will have work', 'work', 'Future Continuous.']],
      dlg: ['Host: Will artificial intelligence take our jobs? Expert: It is widely believed that routine jobs will have been automated by 2040. Host: And creative jobs? Expert: They are less likely to be replaced, but we will be working alongside AI tools. Host: What about bias? Expert: Algorithms can reflect the bias in their data.', 'What can algorithms reflect?', 'The bias in their data', 'The weather', 'The price of oil', 'The expert says “the bias in their data”.'],
      rd: ['Artificial intelligence is advancing faster than many experts predicted. Machine-learning systems can now diagnose diseases, translate languages and write simple reports. Supporters argue that automation will free people from repetitive work and increase productivity. Critics, however, warn that millions of routine jobs may disappear and that algorithms can repeat human bias. Most researchers agree that societies need to retrain workers and set clear rules for how AI is used.', ['What do most researchers agree on?', 'Societies need to retrain workers and set rules', 'AI should be banned', 'AI is harmless'], ['Supporters say automation will create more repetitive work.', 'False'], ['AI was invented in the 1990s.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write 10 sentences predicting how AI will change work in the next 20 years, using Future Perfect and Future Continuous.', 'will have|will be|by 20|automation', 70, 'By 2045, many routine jobs will have been automated. Doctors will be using AI to diagnose diseases faster. Workers will be learning new skills throughout their lives. It is likely that creative jobs will remain safe. However, algorithms may repeat bias, so societies must set clear rules.'],
      sp: ['Say what you think AI will have changed by 2040.', 'By 2040 AI will have changed education and health care. We will be working with it every day.'],
      ts: [['Prejudice built into a system:', 'bias', 'routine', 'algorithm'], ['“Avtomatlashtirish” in English:', 'automation', 'algorithm', 'machine'], ['By 2050, scientists ___ the problem.', 'will have solved', 'will solving', 'solve']] },
    { t: ['Digital privacy', 'Raqamli maxfiylik'],
      obj: ['Raqamli maxfiylik, ma’lumotlarni yig‘ish va kuzatuv haqida fikr yuritasiz.', 'You will reflect on digital privacy, data collection and surveillance.'],
      ex: ['Maxfiylik: data collection, tracking, cookies, surveillance (kuzatuv), consent (rozilik), encryption (shifrlash), personal data, data breach (ma’lumot sizib chiqishi). Majhul va rasmiy uslub: Personal data is collected by most websites. It has been reported that millions of accounts were leaked.\nQarshi fikr: On the one hand…, whereas critics argue that… Daraja: to a certain extent (ma’lum darajada), to a large extent. Majbur: be required to, be obliged to, have no choice but to.', 'Privacy: data collection, tracking, cookies, surveillance, consent, encryption, personal data, data breach. Passive and formal style: Personal data is collected by most websites. It has been reported that millions of accounts were leaked.\nCounter-view: On the one hand…, whereas critics argue that… Degree: to a certain extent, to a large extent. Obligation: be required to, be obliged to, have no choice but to.'],
      eg: [['Personal data is collected by most websites.', 'Shaxsiy ma’lumotlar ko‘pchilik saytlar tomonidan yig‘iladi.'], ['It has been reported that millions of accounts were leaked.', 'Millionlab akkaunt sizib chiqqani xabar qilingan.'], ['To a certain extent, users accept tracking.', 'Ma’lum darajada foydalanuvchilar kuzatuvni qabul qiladi.'], ['Companies are obliged to ask for consent.', 'Kompaniyalar rozilik so‘rashga majbur.']],
      w: [['surveillance', 'kuzatuv', 'слежка', 'noun', 'Surveillance cameras are everywhere.', 'Kuzatuv kameralari hamma joyda.', 'sɜːˈveɪləns'], ['consent', 'rozilik', 'согласие', 'noun', 'You must give your consent.', 'Siz rozilik bildirishingiz kerak.', 'kənˈsent'], ['encryption', 'shifrlash', 'шифрование', 'noun', 'Encryption protects messages.', 'Shifrlash xabarlarni himoya qiladi.', 'ɪnˈkrɪpʃn'], ['breach', 'sizib chiqish / buzilish', 'утечка', 'noun', 'A data breach exposed passwords.', 'Ma’lumot sizib chiqishi parollarni ochib qo‘ydi.', 'briːtʃ'], ['tracking', 'kuzatib borish', 'отслеживание', 'noun', 'Tracking shows ads to users.', 'Kuzatuv foydalanuvchilarga reklama ko‘rsatadi.', 'ˈtrækɪŋ'], ['oblige', 'majbur qilmoq', 'обязывать', 'verb', 'The law obliges firms to protect data.', 'Qonun firmalarni ma’lumotni himoya qilishga majbur qiladi.', 'əˈblaɪdʒ']],
      g: [['Personal data ___ by most websites.', 'is collected', 'collects', 'is collecting', 'Majhul nisbat.'], ['Companies are ___ to ask for consent.', 'obliged', 'oblige', 'obliging', 'be obliged to.']],
      dlg: ['Student: Do you read privacy policies? Teacher: Rarely, and to a certain extent that is a problem. Student: Why? Teacher: Because we often give consent without knowing how our data is used. Student: It has been reported that many apps share data. Teacher: Yes, which is why encryption and clear laws matter.', 'Why does the teacher say it is a problem?', 'People give consent without reading', 'Apps are free', 'Laws are too strict', 'She says “we often give consent without knowing”.'],
      rd: ['Every time we search, shop or scroll, data is collected about us. Companies use it to personalise advertisements, but it can also be sold, leaked or used for surveillance. After several large data breaches, many governments introduced laws that oblige companies to ask for clear consent and to protect personal information. Privacy advocates argue that these rules do not go far enough, whereas business groups claim that excessive regulation slows innovation.', ['What do laws oblige companies to do?', 'Ask for clear consent and protect data', 'Delete all data', 'Stop advertising'], ['Business groups want more regulation.', 'False'], ['The laws were introduced in Asia first.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a discursive paragraph (10 sentences) on whether privacy or convenience is more important online.', 'to a certain extent|on the one hand|whereas|consent', 70, 'Many people believe that convenience is more important than privacy online. On the one hand, personalised services save time. However, data is collected without clear consent. Whereas companies argue that tracking improves services, critics warn about surveillance. To a certain extent, users should protect themselves with strong passwords and encryption.'],
      sp: ['Give your opinion on whether companies should be allowed to track users.', 'In my opinion, companies should always ask for consent before tracking users.'],
      ts: [['Permission given by a person:', 'consent', 'breach', 'bias'], ['“Shifrlash” in English:', 'encryption', 'surveillance', 'tracking'], ['Firms are ___ to protect data.', 'obliged', 'oblige', 'obligation']] },
    { t: ['Remote work', 'Masofaviy ish'],
      obj: ['Masofaviy ishning afzallik, kamchilik va natijalarini baholaysiz.', 'You will evaluate the advantages, disadvantages and effects of remote work.'],
      ex: ['Masofaviy ish: telework, commute (qatnov), flexible hours, isolation, work–life balance, productivity, collaboration, home office. Qiyosiy tuzilmalar: The more flexible the schedule is, the happier employees are. (Ikkilangan qiyosiy.) Not as … as; far / much / slightly + comparative.\nMuhokama: Remote work has several advantages. Firstly, … Furthermore, … However, … Overall, … (pros-cons). Davomiylik: since the pandemic, over the past decade.', 'Remote work: telework, commute, flexible hours, isolation, work–life balance, productivity, collaboration, home office. Comparative structures: The more flexible the schedule is, the happier employees are. Not as … as; far / much / slightly + comparative.\nDiscussion: Remote work has several advantages. Firstly, … Furthermore, … However, … Overall, … Time: since the pandemic, over the past decade.'],
      eg: [['The more flexible the schedule is, the happier employees are.', 'Jadval qanchalik moslashuvchan bo‘lsa, xodimlar shunchalik baxtli.'], ['Remote work saves the time spent on commuting.', 'Masofaviy ish qatnovga ketadigan vaqtni tejaydi.'], ['Isolation is far more common among home workers.', 'Yakkalanish uyda ishlovchilar orasida ancha keng tarqalgan.'], ['Since the pandemic, more people have worked from home.', 'Pandemiyadan beri ko‘proq odam uyda ishlagan.']],
      w: [['commute', 'qatnov (uydan ishga)', 'дорога на работу', 'noun', 'My commute takes an hour.', 'Qatnovim bir soat oladi.', 'kəˈmjuːt'], ['productivity', 'unumdorlik', 'продуктивность', 'noun', 'Productivity increased at home.', 'Uyda unumdorlik oshdi.', 'ˌprɒdʌkˈtɪvəti'], ['collaboration', 'hamkorlikda ishlash', 'сотрудничество', 'noun', 'Collaboration is harder online.', 'Onlayn hamkorlikda ishlash qiyinroq.', 'kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃn'], ['isolation', 'yakkalanish', 'изоляция', 'noun', 'Isolation can affect mental health.', 'Yakkalanish ruhiy salomatlikka ta’sir qilishi mumkin.', 'ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn'], ['flexible', 'moslashuvchan', 'гибкий', 'adjective', 'A flexible schedule helps parents.', 'Moslashuvchan jadval ota-onalarga yordam beradi.', 'ˈfleksəbl'], ['telework', 'masofaviy ishlamoq', 'удалённая работа', 'verb', 'Many staff telework twice a week.', 'Ko‘p xodimlar haftada ikki marta masofadan ishlaydi.', 'ˈtelɪwɜːk']],
      g: [['The more flexible the schedule is, ___ the employees are.', 'the happier', 'happier', 'the happiest', 'Ikkilangan qiyosiy.'], ['Since the pandemic, more people ___ from home.', 'have worked', 'worked', 'are worked', 'Present Perfect — since.']],
      dlg: ['Manager: Shall we allow staff to telework three days a week? HR: The more flexible we are, the more productive they usually are. Manager: But what about collaboration? HR: It is slightly harder online, though meetings can solve that. Manager: And isolation? HR: We can organise office days once a week.', 'How often does HR suggest office days?', 'Once a week', 'Every day', 'Never', 'HR says “once a week”.'],
      rd: ['Since the pandemic, remote work has become a regular option for many employees. Studies show that workers save an average of an hour a day by avoiding the commute and often report higher productivity. On the other hand, isolation and difficulties with collaboration are common complaints, and some people find it harder to separate work from home life. Many companies have therefore adopted a hybrid model, in which staff work from home for part of the week and meet in the office for the rest.', ['What is a hybrid model?', 'Working partly at home and partly in the office', 'Working only in the office', 'Working at night'], ['Remote workers always have a worse work–life balance.', 'False'], ['The study covered 5,000 companies.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a for-and-against paragraph (10–12 sentences) on remote work; include a double comparative.', 'the more|however|firstly|overall', 70, 'Remote work has several advantages. Firstly, it saves commuting time. The more flexible the schedule is, the happier employees are. Furthermore, productivity often increases. However, isolation is a common problem and collaboration can be harder. Overall, a hybrid model seems to combine the best of both worlds.'],
      sp: ['Say whether you would prefer to work from home or in an office and why.', 'I would prefer a hybrid model. The more flexible I am, the more productive I feel.'],
      ts: [['Travel between home and work:', 'commute', 'telework', 'isolation'], ['“Unumdorlik” in English:', 'productivity', 'collaboration', 'flexible'], ['Work is ___ easier at home. (a lot)', 'far', 'so much as', 'very']] },
    { t: ['A technology essay', 'Texnologiya haqida esse'],
      obj: ['Texnologiya mavzusida to‘liq argumentativ esse yozasiz.', 'You will write a full argumentative essay on a technology topic.'],
      ex: ['Argumentativ esse: 1) Kirish — mavzu + tezis (thesis statement): This essay will argue that… 2) 2–3 asosiy paragraf — fikr, tushuntirish, dalil, qarshi fikrga javob. 3) Xulosa — tezisni boshqacha so‘zlar bilan takrorlash + yakuniy fikr. Linkerlar: Firstly/Secondly/Finally; Moreover; Nevertheless; Admittedly (to‘g‘ri, lekin); Thus/Hence; In summary.\nSifat belgilari: neutral rasmiy uslub, qisqartmasiz, ehtiyotkor ifoda (tend to, may), hajm 250–280 so‘z, aniq misollar.',  'Argumentative essay: 1) Introduction — topic + thesis statement: This essay will argue that… 2) 2–3 body paragraphs — point, explanation, evidence, response to the counter-argument. 3) Conclusion — restate the thesis in different words + final thought. Linkers: Firstly/Secondly/Finally; Moreover; Nevertheless; Admittedly; Thus/Hence; In summary.\nStyle: neutral and formal, no contractions, hedging (tend to, may), 250–280 words, concrete examples.'],
      eg: [['This essay will argue that technology improves education.', 'Bu esse texnologiya ta’limni yaxshilashini isbotlaydi.'], ['Admittedly, screens can be distracting.', 'To‘g‘ri, ekranlar chalg‘itishi mumkin.'], ['Nevertheless, the benefits outweigh the risks.', 'Shunday bo‘lsa-da, foydalar xavflardan ustun.'], ['In summary, technology is a tool, not a solution.', 'Xulosa qilib aytganda, texnologiya vosita, yechim emas.']],
      w: [['thesis', 'asosiy tezis', 'тезис', 'noun', 'The thesis is in the first paragraph.', 'Tezis birinchi paragrafda.', 'ˈθiːsɪs'], ['outweigh', 'ustun kelmoq', 'перевешивать', 'verb', 'The benefits outweigh the risks.', 'Foydalar xavflardan ustun.', 'ˌaʊtˈweɪ'], ['admittedly', 'to‘g‘ri, lekin', 'правда', 'adverb', 'Admittedly, it is expensive.', 'To‘g‘ri, qimmat.', 'ədˈmɪtɪdli'], ['evidence', 'dalil', 'доказательство', 'noun', 'Give evidence for your claim.', 'Da’voingiz uchun dalil keltiring.', 'ˈevɪdəns'], ['counter-argument', 'qarshi dalil', 'контраргумент', 'noun', 'Respond to the counter-argument.', 'Qarshi dalilga javob bering.', 'ˈkaʊntər ˈɑːɡjumənt'], ['moreover', 'bundan tashqari', 'более того', 'adverb', 'Moreover, it saves time.', 'Bundan tashqari, vaqtni tejaydi.', 'mɔːrˈəʊvə']],
      g: [['___, screens can be distracting.', 'Admittedly', 'Admittance', 'Admit', 'Ravish kerak.'], ['The benefits ___ the risks.', 'outweigh', 'outweighs', 'outweighing', 'Ko‘plik: outweigh.']],
      dlg: ['Teacher: What belongs in an introduction? Student: The topic and a clear thesis. Teacher: And in the body? Student: Points with evidence, and a response to the counter-argument. Teacher: Good. And the conclusion? Student: A summary in different words, with no new ideas.', 'What should the conclusion avoid?', 'New ideas', 'A summary', 'A final thought', 'The student says “no new ideas”.'],
      rd: ['Technology has transformed education, yet its value is still debated. This essay will argue that, used wisely, it improves learning. Firstly, online resources give students access to knowledge that was once available only to a few. Admittedly, screens can be distracting and some students become dependent on them. Nevertheless, teachers who set clear rules usually find that the benefits outweigh the risks. In summary, technology is a powerful tool whose success depends on how it is used.', ['What is the writer’s thesis?', 'Technology improves learning if used wisely', 'Technology should be banned', 'Teachers are not needed'], ['The writer ignores counter-arguments.', 'False'], ['The writer is a school director.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write an argumentative essay (250–280 words): “Technology does more harm than good.” Discuss and give your opinion.', 'this essay will argue|admittedly|nevertheless|in summary', 180, 'Technology plays an important role in modern life, but some people claim that it does more harm than good. This essay will argue that, on balance, it is beneficial. Firstly, technology improves communication and access to information. Moreover, it makes many jobs safer. Admittedly, it can cause distraction and loss of privacy. Nevertheless, the benefits outweigh the risks if people use it responsibly. In summary, technology is a tool whose value depends on the user.'],
      sp: ['State a thesis about technology and give one supporting reason.', 'I believe technology is mostly beneficial because it gives everyone access to information.'],
      ts: [['The main claim of an essay:', 'thesis', 'evidence', 'counter-argument'], ['“Dalil” in English:', 'evidence', 'thesis', 'consent'], ['___, it is expensive.', 'Admittedly', 'Admitted of', 'Admission']] },
  ], exam: [['By 2050, doctors ___ new methods.', 'will have developed', 'will developing', 'develop', 'grammar'], ['Websites must ask for your ___ before using cookies.', 'consent', 'commute', 'algorithm', 'vocabulary'], ['The ___ you practise, the better you speak.', 'more', 'most', 'many', 'grammar']] },

  { title: 'Psychology and behaviour', lessons: [
    { t: ['Personality and motivation', 'Shaxsiyat va motivatsiya'],
      obj: ['Shaxsiyat turlari va motivatsiya omillarini tavsiflaysiz.', 'You will describe personality types and motivation factors.'],
      ex: ['Shaxsiyat: introvert / extrovert, ambitious (shuhratparast), reliable, outgoing (ochiq), sensitive, determined (qat’iyatli). Motivatsiya: intrinsic (ichki) vs extrinsic (tashqi, masalan pul), goal-setting, reward, persistence.\nO‘zgartirish fe’llari: tend to, be inclined to, be prone to. Passive of perception: He is considered to be ambitious. Modal of deduction: She must be motivated (aniq xulosa); He can’t be shy (mumkin emas); They might be nervous.', 'Personality: introvert / extrovert, ambitious, reliable, outgoing, sensitive, determined. Motivation: intrinsic vs extrinsic (e.g. money), goal-setting, reward, persistence.\nTendency verbs: tend to, be inclined to, be prone to. Passive of perception: He is considered to be ambitious. Modals of deduction: She must be motivated (certain); He can’t be shy (impossible); They might be nervous.'],
      eg: [['He is considered to be extremely ambitious.', 'U juda shuhratparast hisoblanadi.'], ['She must be very motivated to study at night.', 'U kechasi o‘qish uchun juda motivatsiyali bo‘lsa kerak.'], ['Extroverts tend to enjoy meeting new people.', 'Ekstravertlar yangi odamlar bilan tanishishni yoqtirishga moyil.'], ['Intrinsic motivation comes from interest, not rewards.', 'Ichki motivatsiya qiziqishdan keladi, mukofotdan emas.']],
      w: [['ambitious', 'shuhratparast', 'амбициозный', 'adjective', 'She is an ambitious student.', 'U shuhratparast talaba.', 'æmˈbɪʃəs'], ['determined', 'qat’iyatli', 'решительный', 'adjective', 'He is determined to succeed.', 'U muvaffaqiyatga qat’iy intiladi.', 'dɪˈtɜːmɪnd'], ['introvert', 'introvert', 'интроверт', 'noun', 'An introvert needs quiet time.', 'Introvertga sokin vaqt kerak.', 'ˈɪntrəvɜːt'], ['intrinsic', 'ichki (o‘z-o‘zidan)', 'внутренний', 'adjective', 'Intrinsic motivation lasts longer.', 'Ichki motivatsiya uzoqroq davom etadi.', 'ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk'], ['persistence', 'qat’iyat, sabr', 'настойчивость', 'noun', 'Persistence leads to success.', 'Qat’iyat muvaffaqiyatga olib keladi.', 'pəˈsɪstəns'], ['reward', 'mukofot', 'награда', 'noun', 'A reward can motivate people.', 'Mukofot odamlarni rag‘batlantirishi mumkin.', 'rɪˈwɔːd']],
      g: [['She ___ be very motivated to study at night.', 'must', 'can’t', 'might not', 'Aniq xulosa — must.'], ['He ___ to be extremely ambitious.', 'is considered', 'considers', 'is considering', 'Passive of perception.']],
      dlg: ['Psychologist: What motivates you to study? Student: Mainly interest in the subject. Psychologist: That is intrinsic motivation. Student: But I also work for good marks. Psychologist: Extrinsic motivation. You must be quite determined. Student: I tend to set goals every week.', 'What kind of motivation is interest in the subject?', 'Intrinsic', 'Extrinsic', 'None', 'The psychologist says “That is intrinsic motivation”.'],
      rd: ['Psychologists distinguish between intrinsic motivation, which comes from curiosity and enjoyment, and extrinsic motivation, which depends on rewards or fear of punishment. Research suggests that intrinsically motivated learners tend to be more persistent and to remember information longer. However, extrinsic rewards can be useful at the beginning, especially for tasks that are not naturally interesting. Personality also matters: ambitious and determined people usually set clear goals, while sensitive individuals may need more encouragement.', ['Which learners remember information longer?', 'Intrinsically motivated ones', 'Those who fear punishment', 'Those who avoid goals'], ['Extrinsic rewards are never useful.', 'False'], ['Introverts are more intelligent.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Describe the personality of someone you admire and what motivates them (10 sentences), using modals of deduction and tendency verbs.', 'must be|tends to|is considered|intrinsic', 70, 'My uncle is considered to be an extremely determined person. He must be very motivated, because he studies every night. He tends to set clear goals. His motivation is mostly intrinsic: he simply loves learning. He can’t be lazy, as he finishes everything on time.'],
      sp: ['Describe what motivates you to learn English.', 'My motivation is mostly intrinsic: I enjoy languages. I also want a better job, which is extrinsic.'],
      ts: [['Motivation from inside:', 'intrinsic', 'extrinsic', 'routine'], ['“Qat’iyat” in English:', 'persistence', 'reward', 'introvert'], ['He ___ be tired — he just ran ten km.', 'must', 'can’t be', 'might not']] },
    { t: ['Habits and change', 'Odatlar va o‘zgarish'],
      obj: ['Odat shakllanishi va o‘zgartirish strategiyalarini tushuntirasiz.', 'You will explain how habits form and strategies for changing them.'],
      ex: ['Odat: form a habit, break a habit, trigger (qo‘zg‘atuvchi), routine, willpower (irodа), relapse (qaytalanish), gradual (bosqichma-bosqich). Odat haqida gapirish: used to (ilgari odat edi), be used to + -ing (ko‘nikkan), get used to (ko‘nikib bormoq), would (o‘tgan odat).\nMaslahat uchun: The key to changing a habit is to… It helps to…, Rather than + -ing. Shart: As long as, provided that (… sharti bilan).', 'Habit: form a habit, break a habit, trigger, routine, willpower, relapse, gradual. Talking about habits: used to (past), be used to + -ing (accustomed), get used to (become accustomed), would (past habit).\nAdvice: The key to changing a habit is to… It helps to…, Rather than + -ing. Condition: As long as, provided that.'],
      eg: [['I used to bite my nails, but I broke the habit.', 'Ilgari tirnoqlarimni tishlardim, lekin odatni tashladim.'], ['I am used to getting up early.', 'Men erta turishga ko‘nikkanman.'], ['It takes time to get used to a new routine.', 'Yangi tartibga ko‘nikish vaqt oladi.'], ['You will succeed as long as you stay consistent.', 'Izchil bo‘lsangiz, muvaffaqiyatga erishasiz.']],
      w: [['trigger', 'qo‘zg‘atuvchi', 'триггер', 'noun', 'Stress is a trigger for snacking.', 'Stress gazak yeyishni qo‘zg‘atadi.', 'ˈtrɪɡə'], ['willpower', 'iroda kuchi', 'сила воли', 'noun', 'Willpower is limited.', 'Iroda kuchi cheklangan.', 'ˈwɪlpaʊə'], ['relapse', 'qaytalanish', 'рецидив', 'noun', 'A relapse is normal.', 'Qaytalanish oddiy hol.', 'ˈriːlæps'], ['gradual', 'bosqichma-bosqich', 'постепенный', 'adjective', 'Gradual change lasts.', 'Bosqichma-bosqich o‘zgarish saqlanadi.', 'ˈɡrædʒuəl'], ['consistent', 'izchil', 'последовательный', 'adjective', 'Be consistent every day.', 'Har kuni izchil bo‘ling.', 'kənˈsɪstənt'], ['routine', 'kun tartibi', 'распорядок', 'noun', 'A routine saves energy.', 'Kun tartibi energiyani tejaydi.', 'ruːˈtiːn']],
      g: [['I am ___ to getting up early.', 'used', 'use', 'using', '“be used to + -ing”.'], ['It takes time to get used ___ a new routine.', 'to', 'for', 'with', '“get used to”.']],
      dlg: ['Coach: What habit would you like to change? Ali: I used to go to bed early, but now I stay up late. Coach: What triggers it? Ali: Scrolling on my phone. Coach: Rather than relying on willpower, put the phone in another room. It helps to change the environment. Ali: I’ll try that and stay consistent.', 'What does the coach suggest?', 'Put the phone in another room', 'Buy a new phone', 'Sleep less', 'The coach says “put the phone in another room”.'],
      rd: ['It is often said that it takes twenty-one days to form a habit, but research suggests that the average is closer to two months. What matters most is consistency: repeating a behaviour in the same situation until it becomes automatic. Psychologists recommend identifying the trigger of a bad habit and replacing the response with a healthier one. Relapses should not be seen as failure; rather, they are a normal part of gradual change, provided that the person returns to the routine.', ['What matters most in forming a habit?', 'Consistency', 'Speed', 'Luck'], ['It always takes exactly 21 days.', 'False'], ['The study was done in Japan.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write 10 sentences about a habit you formed or broke: what you used to do, what triggered it and what helped you change.', 'used to|trigger|get used to|as long as', 70, 'I used to stay up late every night. The trigger was scrolling on my phone. At first it was hard to get used to going to bed early. Rather than relying on willpower, I put my phone in another room. As long as I stay consistent, I sleep better. Now I am used to waking up at six.'],
      sp: ['Talk about a habit you want to change and how.', 'I want to stop checking my phone so often. I will put it away while I study.'],
      ts: [['Something that starts a habit:', 'trigger', 'relapse', 'reward'], ['“Bosqichma-bosqich” in English:', 'gradual', 'consistent', 'routine'], ['I’m not used ___ working at night.', 'to', 'for', 'in']] },
    { t: ['Memory and learning', 'Xotira va o‘rganish'],
      obj: ['Xotira va samarali o‘rganish strategiyalarini tavsiflaysiz.', 'You will describe memory and effective learning strategies.'],
      ex: ['Xotira: short-term / long-term memory, recall (eslab qolmoq), retain (saqlab qolmoq), forget, memorise, revise, spaced repetition (oraliqli takrorlash), association. Strategiyalar: mnemonics, mind maps, self-testing. Fe’l + -ing/to: remember doing (qilganini eslamoq) vs remember to do (qilishni unutmaslik); forget doing / to do; stop doing / to do; try doing / to do.\nAniqlik: Studies show that…, According to research…, This suggests that… (ehtiyotkor xulosa).', 'Memory: short-term / long-term memory, recall, retain, forget, memorise, revise, spaced repetition, association. Strategies: mnemonics, mind maps, self-testing. Verb + -ing/to: remember doing vs remember to do; forget doing / to do; stop doing / to do; try doing / to do.\nEvidence: Studies show that…, According to research…, This suggests that… (cautious conclusion).'],
      eg: [['I remember learning this word last week.', 'Bu so‘zni o‘tgan hafta o‘rganganim esimda.'], ['Remember to revise before the exam.', 'Imtihondan oldin takrorlashni unutmang.'], ['Spaced repetition helps to retain information.', 'Oraliqli takrorlash ma’lumotni saqlashga yordam beradi.'], ['This suggests that testing yourself works.', 'Bu o‘z-o‘zini sinash samarali ekanini ko‘rsatadi.']],
      w: [['recall', 'eslab qolmoq', 'вспоминать', 'verb', 'I can’t recall his name.', 'Uning ismini eslay olmayapman.', 'rɪˈkɔːl'], ['retain', 'saqlab qolmoq', 'удерживать', 'verb', 'We retain more when we practise.', 'Mashq qilsak, ko‘proq saqlab qolamiz.', 'rɪˈteɪn'], ['memorise', 'yodlamoq', 'запоминать', 'verb', 'Memorise ten words a day.', 'Kuniga o‘nta so‘z yodlang.', 'ˈmeməraɪz'], ['mnemonic', 'esda tutish usuli', 'мнемоника', 'noun', 'A mnemonic helps me remember.', 'Esda tutish usuli eslab qolishga yordam beradi.', 'nɪˈmɒnɪk'], ['association', 'bog‘lanish', 'ассоциация', 'noun', 'Make an association with a picture.', 'Rasm bilan bog‘lang.', 'əˌsəʊsiˈeɪʃn'], ['self-testing', 'o‘zini sinash', 'самопроверка', 'noun', 'Self-testing improves memory.', 'O‘zini sinash xotirani yaxshilaydi.', 'self ˈtestɪŋ']],
      g: [['Remember ___ revise before the exam.', 'to', 'revising', 'for', '“remember to” — majburiyatni unutmaslik.'], ['I remember ___ this word last week.', 'learning', 'to learn', 'learn', '“remember -ing” — o‘tgan voqea.']],
      dlg: ['Tutor: How do you memorise vocabulary? Student: I just read the list several times. Tutor: Studies show that self-testing works better. Try covering the words and recalling them. Student: And how often should I revise? Tutor: Use spaced repetition: after a day, a week and a month.', 'What works better than reading a list?', 'Self-testing', 'Reading louder', 'Writing once', 'She says “self-testing works better”.'],
      rd: ['Memory is not a single system. Information first enters short-term memory, where it stays for only seconds unless it is rehearsed. Through repetition and meaningful association, some of it moves into long-term memory. Research indicates that spreading revision over several days, known as spaced repetition, helps learners retain far more than a single long session. Mnemonics, mind maps and self-testing are additional tools that make recall easier.', ['Which approach helps learners retain more?', 'Spaced repetition', 'A single long session', 'Reading only once'], ['Short-term memory lasts for years.', 'False'], ['Mind maps were invented in 1970.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write an advice text (10 sentences) for a new learner on how to memorise vocabulary effectively.', 'spaced repetition|self-testing|remember to|studies show', 70, 'To memorise vocabulary effectively, you should use spaced repetition. Studies show that revising after a day, a week and a month helps you retain more. Try self-testing instead of just rereading. Remember to link new words with pictures or stories. A mnemonic can also make recall easier.'],
      sp: ['Explain your best method for remembering new words.', 'I write new words on cards and test myself every day. I remember using them in sentences better.'],
      ts: [['Keeping information over time:', 'retain', 'recall', 'forget'], ['“Yodlamoq” in English:', 'memorise', 'retain', 'recall'], ['I stopped ___ at the shop for water.', 'to buy', 'buying', 'bought']] },
    { t: ['Writing a behaviour report', 'Xulq-atvor hisobotini yozish'],
      obj: ['Kuzatuv asosida rasmiy hisobot yozasiz.', 'You will write a formal report based on observation.'],
      ex: ['Hisobot tuzilmasi: Title → Introduction (maqsad) → Findings (topilmalar, sarlavhalar bilan) → Conclusion → Recommendations. Uslub: rasmiy, majhul, qisqartmasiz. Iboralar: The aim of this report is to… It was found that… The results indicate that… A majority (ko‘pchilik) of respondents… Approximately 60 per cent…\nTavsiyalar: It is recommended that + fe’l (should yoki asosiy shakl): It is recommended that schools introduce…; I would suggest + -ing. Statistik so‘z: a significant proportion, the vast majority, a small minority.', 'Report structure: Title → Introduction (aim) → Findings (with headings) → Conclusion → Recommendations. Style: formal, passive, no contractions. Phrases: The aim of this report is to… It was found that… The results indicate that… A majority of respondents… Approximately 60 per cent…\nRecommendations: It is recommended that + base verb (or should): It is recommended that schools introduce…; I would suggest + -ing. Quantity: a significant proportion, the vast majority, a small minority.'],
      eg: [['The aim of this report is to examine students’ study habits.', 'Bu hisobotning maqsadi — talabalarning o‘qish odatlarini o‘rganish.'], ['It was found that most students revise at night.', 'Ko‘pchilik talabalar kechasi takrorlashi aniqlandi.'], ['The results indicate that sleep affects performance.', 'Natijalar uyqu natijalarga ta’sir qilishini ko‘rsatadi.'], ['It is recommended that schools start later.', 'Maktablar keyinroq boshlashi tavsiya etiladi.']],
      w: [['respondent', 'so‘rovda qatnashuvchi', 'респондент', 'noun', 'Most respondents agreed.', 'Ko‘pchilik so‘rovda qatnashuvchi rozi bo‘ldi.', 'rɪˈspɒndənt'], ['survey', 'so‘rovnoma', 'опрос', 'noun', 'The survey covered 200 students.', 'So‘rovnoma 200 talabani qamrab oldi.', 'ˈsɜːveɪ'], ['findings', 'topilmalar', 'результаты', 'noun', 'The findings are clear.', 'Topilmalar aniq.', 'ˈfaɪndɪŋz'], ['proportion', 'ulush', 'доля', 'noun', 'A large proportion agreed.', 'Katta ulush rozi bo‘ldi.', 'prəˈpɔːʃn'], ['recommendation', 'tavsiya', 'рекомендация', 'noun', 'The report ends with recommendations.', 'Hisobot tavsiyalar bilan tugaydi.', 'ˌrekəmenˈdeɪʃn'], ['indicate', 'ko‘rsatmoq', 'указывать', 'verb', 'The data indicate a trend.', 'Ma’lumotlar tendensiyani ko‘rsatadi.', 'ˈɪndɪkeɪt']],
      g: [['It is recommended that schools ___ later.', 'start', 'starts', 'started', 'Taklif: that + asosiy shakl.'], ['It ___ found that most students revise at night.', 'was', 'were', 'is finding', 'Majhul.']],
      dlg: ['Supervisor: Did you finish the report? Student: Yes. The aim was to examine study habits. Supervisor: What did the survey find? Student: A significant proportion of respondents revise late at night. Supervisor: And your recommendation? Student: It is recommended that students plan a regular schedule.', 'What is recommended?', 'A regular schedule', 'More homework', 'Fewer tests', 'The student says “a regular schedule”.'],
      rd: ['Report on Student Sleep Habits. Introduction: The aim of this report is to examine how much sleep students get. Findings: A survey of 150 students showed that the vast majority sleep fewer than seven hours on school nights. A significant proportion reported difficulty concentrating in morning lessons. Conclusion: The results indicate that lack of sleep may reduce performance. Recommendations: It is recommended that the school start lessons later and run workshops on healthy sleep.', ['What is the aim of the report?', 'To examine how much sleep students get', 'To test teachers', 'To buy beds'], ['Most students sleep more than eight hours.', 'False'], ['The survey was carried out in a village.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a short formal report (200 words) on the study or sleep habits of your classmates (invented but realistic data).', 'the aim of this report|it was found|the results indicate|it is recommended', 130, 'Report on Study Habits. Introduction: The aim of this report is to examine how students prepare for exams. Findings: A survey of 100 students showed that a majority revise during the final week. It was found that a small minority use spaced repetition. Conclusion: The results indicate that many students could study more effectively. Recommendations: It is recommended that teachers introduce lessons on study skills.'],
      sp: ['Present the main finding of a survey in two sentences.', 'The survey found that most students sleep less than seven hours. It is recommended that lessons start later.'],
      ts: [['Words used to report results:', 'The findings indicate…', 'Guess what!', 'Dear Sir'], ['“So‘rovnoma” in English:', 'survey', 'finding', 'proportion'], ['It is recommended that she ___ more.', 'sleep', 'sleeps', 'slept']] },
  ], exam: [['She ___ be nervous — her hands are shaking.', 'must', 'can’t', 'mustn’t', 'grammar'], ['It takes time to get used ___ a new routine.', 'to', 'at', 'on', 'grammar'], ['A small trigger that starts a habit:', 'trigger', 'relapse', 'proportion', 'vocabulary']] },

  { title: 'Education and learning', lessons: [
    { t: ['Learning styles', 'O‘rganish uslublari'],
      obj: ['Turli o‘rganish uslublarini tavsiflab, o‘zingizga mosini asoslaysiz.', 'You will describe different learning styles and justify the one that suits you.'],
      ex: ['Uslublar: visual (ko‘rish), auditory (eshitish), kinaesthetic (harakat orqali), reading/writing learners. Qarama-qarshi fikr: Although the theory is popular, there is little scientific evidence that…. Nisbiy gap (non-defining): Visual learners, who prefer diagrams, often use colours.\nQo‘shma gap: prefer + ot / -ing / to; would rather + asosiy fe’l. Tahlil iboralari: be suited to, benefit from, cater for (… ga moslashmoq), a one-size-fits-all approach.', 'Styles: visual, auditory, kinaesthetic, reading/writing learners. Contrast: Although the theory is popular, there is little scientific evidence that…. Non-defining relative: Visual learners, who prefer diagrams, often use colours.\nPatterns: prefer + noun / -ing / to; would rather + base verb. Analysis phrases: be suited to, benefit from, cater for, a one-size-fits-all approach.'],
      eg: [['Visual learners, who prefer diagrams, often use colours.', 'Ko‘rish orqali o‘rganuvchilar, diagrammalarni afzal ko‘radi, ko‘pincha ranglardan foydalanadi.'], ['I would rather listen to a lecture than read a book.', 'Kitob o‘qigandan ko‘ra ma’ruza tinglaganni afzal ko‘raman.'], ['Teachers should cater for different needs.', 'O‘qituvchilar turli ehtiyojlarga moslashishi kerak.'], ['A one-size-fits-all approach rarely works.', 'Hamma uchun bir xil yondashuv kamdan-kam ishlaydi.']],
      w: [['visual', 'ko‘rish orqali', 'визуальный', 'adjective', 'I am a visual learner.', 'Men ko‘rish orqali o‘rganaman.', 'ˈvɪʒuəl'], ['auditory', 'eshitish orqali', 'слуховой', 'adjective', 'Auditory learners enjoy podcasts.', 'Eshitish orqali o‘rganuvchilar podkastni yoqtiradi.', 'ˈɔːdətri'], ['kinaesthetic', 'harakat orqali', 'кинестетический', 'adjective', 'Kinaesthetic learners learn by doing.', 'Harakat orqali o‘rganuvchilar qilib o‘rganadi.', 'ˌkɪnəsˈθetɪk'], ['cater for', 'moslashmoq, ehtiyojni qondirmoq', 'учитывать потребности', 'phrasal verb', 'Schools should cater for all pupils.', 'Maktablar barcha o‘quvchilarni hisobga olishi kerak.', 'ˈkeɪtə fɔː'], ['preference', 'afzal ko‘rish', 'предпочтение', 'noun', 'It is a personal preference.', 'Bu shaxsiy afzallik.', 'ˈprefrəns'], ['evidence', 'ilmiy dalil', 'доказательства', 'noun', 'There is little evidence for it.', 'Buning uchun dalil kam.', 'ˈevɪdəns']],
      g: [['I would rather ___ to a lecture than read a book.', 'listen', 'listening', 'to listen', 'would rather + asosiy fe’l.'], ['Visual learners, ___ prefer diagrams, use colours.', 'who', 'which', 'whose', 'Odamlar — who.']],
      dlg: ['Teacher: What kind of learner are you? Ali: Probably visual. I remember diagrams better than words. Teacher: Many people say that, although there is little scientific evidence for fixed styles. Ali: So a one-size-fits-all approach is not ideal? Teacher: Exactly. Good teaching caters for different needs.', 'What does the teacher say about learning styles?', 'There is little scientific evidence for fixed styles', 'They are proven', 'They are useless', 'She says “little scientific evidence”.'],
      rd: ['The idea that people learn best in a single style, visual, auditory or kinaesthetic, became hugely popular in schools. Yet researchers who have tested the theory found that students did not learn better when teaching matched their supposed style. What does help is variety: explaining a concept in words, pictures and practice engages more memory systems. Consequently, many educators now recommend a flexible approach that caters for different preferences rather than labelling pupils.', ['What helps learning, according to the text?', 'Variety in how a concept is presented', 'Matching a single fixed style', 'Avoiding pictures'], ['Researchers confirmed that matching styles improves results.', 'False'], ['Most schools have abolished the theory.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write 10 sentences on how you learn best and whether teachers should cater for learning styles.', 'i would rather|prefer|although|cater for', 70, 'I learn best when I can see information in diagrams. I would rather watch a short video than read a long text. Although the theory of learning styles is popular, there is little evidence that it improves results. Teachers should cater for different needs by using variety. A one-size-fits-all approach rarely works.'],
      sp: ['Say how you prefer to learn new words and why.', 'I prefer learning new words with pictures. It is easier for me to remember them.'],
      ts: [['Learning by doing:', 'kinaesthetic', 'auditory', 'visual'], ['“Afzal ko‘rish” in English:', 'preference', 'evidence', 'approach'], ['She ___ rather study alone.', 'would', 'is', 'does']] },
    { t: ['Education systems', 'Ta’lim tizimlari'],
      obj: ['Turli mamlakatlar ta’lim tizimlarini solishtirasiz va baholaysiz.', 'You will compare and evaluate education systems of different countries.'],
      ex: ['Tizim so‘zlari: primary / secondary / tertiary education, curriculum (o‘quv dasturi), compulsory (majburiy), tuition fees (o‘qish to‘lovi), standardised tests, vocational training (kasb-hunar). Taqqoslash: whereas, while, in contrast, similarly, compared with, on the other hand.\nMajhul va rasmiy: Education is compulsory until sixteen. Students are required to…. Hedging: This system appears to…, seems to…, tends to… Kamsituvchi/oshiruvchi: considerably, slightly, significantly more …',  'System words: primary / secondary / tertiary education, curriculum, compulsory, tuition fees, standardised tests, vocational training. Comparing: whereas, while, in contrast, similarly, compared with, on the other hand.\nPassive: Education is compulsory until sixteen. Students are required to…. Hedging: This system appears to…, seems to…, tends to… Degree: considerably, slightly, significantly more …'],
      eg: [['Education is compulsory until the age of sixteen.', 'Ta’lim o‘n olti yoshgacha majburiy.'], ['Finland has a considerably shorter school day than many countries.', 'Finlyandiyada maktab kuni ko‘p mamlakatlarga qaraganda ancha qisqa.'], ['In contrast, some countries rely heavily on standardised tests.', 'Aksincha, ba’zi mamlakatlar standart testlarga qattiq tayanadi.'], ['Vocational training prepares students for specific jobs.', 'Kasb-hunar ta’limi talabalarni aniq ishlarga tayyorlaydi.']],
      w: [['curriculum', 'o‘quv dasturi', 'учебная программа', 'noun', 'The curriculum includes science.', 'O‘quv dasturiga fan kiradi.', 'kəˈrɪkjələm'], ['compulsory', 'majburiy', 'обязательный', 'adjective', 'School is compulsory.', 'Maktab majburiy.', 'kəmˈpʌlsəri'], ['tuition', 'o‘qish (to‘lovi)', 'обучение', 'noun', 'Tuition fees are high.', 'O‘qish to‘lovlari yuqori.', 'tjuˈɪʃn'], ['vocational', 'kasb-hunarga oid', 'профессиональный', 'adjective', 'Vocational courses train mechanics.', 'Kasb-hunar kurslari mexaniklarni tayyorlaydi.', 'vəʊˈkeɪʃənl'], ['tertiary', 'oliy (uchinchi bosqich)', 'высшее', 'adjective', 'Tertiary education includes universities.', 'Oliy ta’limga universitetlar kiradi.', 'ˈtɜːʃəri'], ['standardised', 'standartlashtirilgan', 'стандартизированный', 'adjective', 'Standardised tests are controversial.', 'Standart testlar munozarali.', 'ˈstændədaɪzd']],
      g: [['Education ___ compulsory until sixteen.', 'is', 'are', 'does', 'Birlik.'], ['___ contrast, some countries rely on tests.', 'In', 'On', 'At', '“In contrast”.']],
      dlg: ['Student A: In my country, education is compulsory until sixteen. Student B: In mine it’s eighteen. Student A: Whereas tuition fees at universities are low in your country, they are considerably higher in mine. Student B: That seems to affect who can study. Student A: Yes, vocational training is an alternative.', 'What is an alternative to university?', 'Vocational training', 'Tuition fees', 'Standardised tests', 'A says “vocational training is an alternative”.'],
      rd: ['Education systems differ widely. In some countries pupils sit national exams at the end of every stage, whereas in others teachers assess students continuously. Finland, which is often praised, has no standardised tests until the end of upper secondary school and a relatively short school day. By contrast, several East Asian systems emphasise long hours and competitive exams, producing very high results but also considerable stress. Experts therefore argue that no single model is ideal; the best systems balance achievement with well-being.', ['What do experts conclude?', 'The best systems balance achievement with well-being', 'One model is ideal', 'Exams should be removed everywhere'], ['Finland uses standardised tests every year.', 'False'], ['Finland spends the most money on schools.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Compare two education systems you know (10–12 sentences) using contrast linkers and hedging.', 'whereas|in contrast|compared with|tends to', 70, 'The education system in my country differs from that in Finland. Education is compulsory until sixteen in my country, whereas in Finland it is similar. Compared with Finland, our school day is longer. Our system tends to rely on exams. In contrast, Finnish schools use more continuous assessment.'],
      sp: ['Compare school in your country with school in another country.', 'In my country school is compulsory until sixteen. In contrast, in some countries it is until eighteen.'],
      ts: [['Training for a specific job:', 'vocational', 'compulsory', 'tertiary'], ['“O‘quv dasturi” in English:', 'curriculum', 'tuition', 'preference'], ['Primary, secondary and ___ education.', 'tertiary', 'tertiarily', 'tertiaries']] },
    { t: ['Online learning', 'Onlayn ta’lim'],
      obj: ['Onlayn ta’limning samaradorligi va muammolarini baholaysiz.', 'You will assess the effectiveness and challenges of online learning.'],
      ex: ['Onlayn ta’lim: e-learning, virtual classroom, self-paced (o‘z sur’atida), drop-out rate, accessibility, interaction, feedback, discipline. Shartli: Second conditional: If online courses were cheaper, more people would enrol. Mixed: If I had studied online, I would be more flexible now.\nTahlil: One advantage of… is that…, A major drawback is that…, This is particularly true for…, It depends on whether… Ma’no: allow / enable / make it possible for somebody to…',  'E-learning: e-learning, virtual classroom, self-paced, drop-out rate, accessibility, interaction, feedback, discipline. Second conditional: If online courses were cheaper, more people would enrol. Mixed: If I had studied online, I would be more flexible now.\nAnalysis: One advantage of… is that…, A major drawback is that…, This is particularly true for…, It depends on whether… Meaning: allow / enable / make it possible for somebody to…'],
      eg: [['If online courses were cheaper, more people would enrol.', 'Onlayn kurslar arzonroq bo‘lsa, ko‘proq odam yozilgan bo‘lardi.'], ['One advantage of e-learning is that it is self-paced.', 'Onlayn ta’limning bir afzalligi — o‘z sur’atida o‘rganish.'], ['A major drawback is the high drop-out rate.', 'Katta kamchilik — o‘qishni tashlab ketishning yuqori darajasi.'], ['Technology makes it possible for rural students to study.', 'Texnologiya qishloq o‘quvchilariga o‘qish imkonini beradi.']],
      w: [['enrol', 'ro‘yxatdan o‘tmoq', 'записываться', 'verb', 'She enrolled on a course.', 'U kursga yozildi.', 'ɪnˈrəʊl'], ['self-paced', 'o‘z sur’atida', 'в своём темпе', 'adjective', 'Self-paced courses are flexible.', 'O‘z sur’atidagi kurslar moslashuvchan.', 'self peɪst'], ['drop-out', 'o‘qishni tashlab ketish', 'отсев', 'noun', 'The drop-out rate is high.', 'O‘qishni tashlab ketish darajasi yuqori.', 'ˈdrɒp aʊt'], ['accessible', 'kirish mumkin bo‘lgan', 'доступный', 'adjective', 'Online lessons are accessible.', 'Onlayn darslarga kirish oson.', 'əkˈsesəbl'], ['interaction', 'o‘zaro muloqot', 'взаимодействие', 'noun', 'Interaction is limited online.', 'Onlaynda muloqot cheklangan.', 'ˌɪntərˈækʃn'], ['discipline', 'intizom', 'дисциплина', 'noun', 'Online study needs discipline.', 'Onlayn o‘qish intizom talab qiladi.', 'ˈdɪsəplɪn']],
      g: [['If courses ___ cheaper, more people would enrol.', 'were', 'are', 'will be', 'Second conditional.'], ['Technology ___ it possible for students to study abroad.', 'makes', 'let', 'allows', '“makes it possible for”.']],
      dlg: ['Tutor: Why did you choose an online course? Ali: It is self-paced and I can study after work. Tutor: What is the biggest challenge? Ali: Discipline. If I were more organised, I would finish faster. Tutor: A major drawback is the drop-out rate, which is high because of limited interaction.', 'What is Ali’s biggest challenge?', 'Discipline', 'Price', 'Technology', 'He says “Discipline”.'],
      rd: ['Online learning has opened education to millions who could not attend traditional classes. It is accessible, often cheaper and self-paced, which suits working adults. However, completion rates are low: in some free courses, fewer than ten per cent of enrolled learners finish. Researchers link this to a lack of interaction and feedback. Courses that include live sessions, deadlines and discussion forums show considerably better results, suggesting that technology works best when combined with human support.', ['What improves completion rates?', 'Live sessions, deadlines and forums', 'Longer videos', 'Cheaper courses'], ['Most free courses are finished by 90% of learners.', 'False'], ['Online courses are always free.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write an evaluation (10–12 sentences) of online learning: advantages, drawbacks and one condition that makes it effective.', 'one advantage|a major drawback|if|it depends on', 70, 'One advantage of online learning is that it is self-paced. Technology makes it possible for people in rural areas to study. However, a major drawback is the limited interaction. If students were given more feedback, they would drop out less often. Ultimately, it depends on whether learners have enough discipline.'],
      sp: ['Say whether you prefer online or classroom learning and give two reasons.', 'I prefer classroom learning because there is more interaction. However, online courses are more flexible.'],
      ts: [['Leaving a course before finishing:', 'drop-out', 'enrol', 'discipline'], ['“Intizom” in English:', 'discipline', 'interaction', 'feedback'], ['If I ___ more time, I would study online.', 'had', 'have', 'will have']] },
    { t: ['An education essay', 'Ta’lim haqida esse'],
      obj: ['Ta’lim mavzusida muammo–yechim yoki fikr esse yozasiz.', 'You will write a problem–solution or opinion essay on education.'],
      ex: ['Muammo–yechim esse: Kirish (muammo + tezis) → 1-asosiy paragraf: muammolar va sabablar → 2-asosiy paragraf: yechimlar va natijalar → Xulosa. Iboralar: One of the main problems is…, This is mainly caused by…, A possible solution would be to…, This would help to…, If this were implemented,… Natija: This would lead to… as well as…\nBog‘lovchilar: not only … but also, as well as, in addition to + -ing, thereby (shu orqali).',  'Problem–solution essay: Introduction (problem + thesis) → Body 1: problems and causes → Body 2: solutions and results → Conclusion. Phrases: One of the main problems is…, This is mainly caused by…, A possible solution would be to…, This would help to…, If this were implemented,… Result: This would lead to… as well as…\nConnectors: not only … but also, as well as, in addition to + -ing, thereby.'],
      eg: [['One of the main problems is overcrowded classrooms.', 'Asosiy muammolardan biri — tig‘iz sinflar.'], ['A possible solution would be to hire more teachers.', 'Mumkin yechim — ko‘proq o‘qituvchi yollash.'], ['This would help to improve individual attention.', 'Bu individual e’tiborni yaxshilashga yordam beradi.'], ['In addition to hiring teachers, schools could use technology.', 'O‘qituvchilar yollashdan tashqari, maktablar texnologiyadan foydalanishi mumkin.']],
      w: [['overcrowded', 'haddan tashqari gavjum', 'переполненный', 'adjective', 'The classrooms are overcrowded.', 'Sinflar haddan tashqari gavjum.', 'ˌəʊvəˈkraʊdɪd'], ['implement', 'amalga oshirmoq', 'внедрять', 'verb', 'Schools should implement the plan.', 'Maktablar rejani amalga oshirishi kerak.', 'ˈɪmplɪment'], ['funding', 'moliyalashtirish', 'финансирование', 'noun', 'Funding for schools is low.', 'Maktablarni moliyalashtirish past.', 'ˈfʌndɪŋ'], ['thereby', 'shu orqali', 'тем самым', 'adverb', 'Smaller classes, thereby improving results.', 'Kichik sinflar, shu orqali natijalar yaxshilanadi.', 'ðeəˈbaɪ'], ['shortage', 'yetishmovchilik', 'нехватка', 'noun', 'There is a shortage of teachers.', 'O‘qituvchilar yetishmaydi.', 'ˈʃɔːtɪdʒ'], ['attention', 'e’tibor', 'внимание', 'noun', 'Pupils need individual attention.', 'O‘quvchilarga individual e’tibor kerak.', 'əˈtenʃn']],
      g: [['If this plan ___ implemented, results would improve.', 'were', 'is', 'would be', 'Second conditional majhul: were implemented.'], ['A possible solution ___ be to hire more teachers.', 'would', 'will have', 'did', 'Ehtiyotkor ifoda: would be.']],
      dlg: ['Teacher: What is the main problem in your school? Student: Overcrowded classrooms. Teacher: And its cause? Student: A shortage of teachers and funding. Teacher: A possible solution would be to hire more staff. Student: That would give pupils more attention.', 'What is a possible solution?', 'Hire more staff', 'Close the school', 'Cancel exams', 'The teacher says “hire more staff”.'],
      rd: ['One of the main problems in many schools is overcrowded classrooms. This is mainly caused by a shortage of teachers and insufficient funding. As a result, pupils receive less individual attention and their results suffer. A possible solution would be to train more teachers and to allocate a larger share of the budget to education. If this were implemented, class sizes would fall, thereby improving both results and well-being.', ['What is a possible solution?', 'Train more teachers and increase funding', 'Reduce lessons', 'Build more prisons'], ['The problem is caused by too many teachers.', 'False'], ['The essay is about a university.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a problem–solution essay (250 words): “Many schools lack resources. What problems does this cause and what can be done?”', 'one of the main problems|a possible solution|would help|if', 180, 'Many schools around the world suffer from a lack of resources. One of the main problems is overcrowded classrooms, which is mainly caused by a shortage of teachers. As a result, pupils receive less individual attention. A possible solution would be to train more teachers and to increase funding. If this were implemented, class sizes would fall. In addition to hiring staff, schools could use technology to support learning. In conclusion, investment in education would benefit the whole society.'],
      sp: ['Present one problem in education and one solution in four sentences.', 'One of the main problems is overcrowded classrooms. A possible solution would be to hire more teachers. This would give pupils more attention.'],
      ts: [['Lack of something:', 'shortage', 'funding', 'attention'], ['“Amalga oshirmoq” in English:', 'implement', 'enrol', 'allocate'], ['It would help ___ the problem.', 'to solve', 'solving the', 'solved']] },
  ], exam: [['She would rather ___ at home than go out.', 'stay', 'staying', 'to stay', 'grammar'], ['If tuition were free, more students ___.', 'would enrol', 'enrolled', 'will enrol', 'grammar'], ['Learning by listening is called ___ learning.', 'auditory', 'visual', 'kinaesthetic', 'vocabulary']] },

  { title: 'Economy and work', lessons: [
    { t: ['Economic terms', 'Iqtisodiy atamalar'],
      obj: ['Asosiy iqtisodiy atamalarni tushunib, ulardan to‘g‘ri foydalanasiz.', 'You will understand and correctly use key economic terms.'],
      ex: ['Atamalar: inflation (inflyatsiya), GDP (YaIM), recession (turg‘unlik), interest rate, supply and demand, trade deficit, budget, tax revenue, exchange rate, unemployment rate. Tahlil fe’llari: rise, fall, remain stable, fluctuate, peak at, plummet; sifat: sharp, gradual, steady.\nTendensiyani tasvirlash: Inflation rose sharply from 2% to 8%. Demand outstripped supply. Majhul: Interest rates are set by the central bank. Bog‘lovchi: as a result of, owing to, due to.', 'Terms: inflation, GDP, recession, interest rate, supply and demand, trade deficit, budget, tax revenue, exchange rate, unemployment rate. Verbs for change: rise, fall, remain stable, fluctuate, peak at, plummet; adjectives: sharp, gradual, steady.\nDescribing trends: Inflation rose sharply from 2% to 8%. Demand outstripped supply. Passive: Interest rates are set by the central bank. Cause: as a result of, owing to, due to.'],
      eg: [['Inflation rose sharply from 2% to 8%.', 'Inflyatsiya 2% dan 8% gacha keskin oshdi.'], ['Interest rates are set by the central bank.', 'Foiz stavkalarini markaziy bank belgilaydi.'], ['The economy fell into recession.', 'Iqtisodiyot turg‘unlikka tushdi.'], ['Demand outstripped supply, so prices went up.', 'Talab taklifdan oshib ketdi, narxlar oshdi.']],
      w: [['inflation', 'inflyatsiya', 'инфляция', 'noun', 'Inflation reduces buying power.', 'Inflyatsiya xarid qobiliyatini kamaytiradi.', 'ɪnˈfleɪʃn'], ['recession', 'turg‘unlik', 'рецессия', 'noun', 'The country entered a recession.', 'Mamlakat turg‘unlikka kirdi.', 'rɪˈseʃn'], ['revenue', 'daromad (davlat)', 'доход', 'noun', 'Tax revenue increased.', 'Soliq daromadi oshdi.', 'ˈrevənjuː'], ['fluctuate', 'tebranmoq', 'колебаться', 'verb', 'Prices fluctuate daily.', 'Narxlar har kuni tebranadi.', 'ˈflʌktʃueɪt'], ['plummet', 'keskin tushmoq', 'резко падать', 'verb', 'Share prices plummeted.', 'Aksiya narxlari keskin tushdi.', 'ˈplʌmɪt'], ['deficit', 'kamomad', 'дефицит', 'noun', 'The trade deficit widened.', 'Savdo kamomadi kengaydi.', 'ˈdefɪsɪt']],
      g: [['Inflation ___ sharply last year.', 'rose', 'raised', 'risen', 'rise (o‘z.) — rose.'], ['Interest rates ___ by the central bank.', 'are set', 'set', 'are setting', 'Majhul.']],
      dlg: ['Analyst: Inflation rose sharply from 2% to 8% owing to higher energy prices. Presenter: What did the central bank do? Analyst: It raised interest rates to slow demand. Presenter: Will there be a recession? Analyst: It is possible, as growth has remained weak and the trade deficit has widened.', 'Why did the bank raise interest rates?', 'To slow demand', 'To increase imports', 'To lower taxes', 'The analyst says “to slow demand”.'],
      rd: ['Economists measure the health of an economy using several indicators. Gross domestic product shows the total value of goods and services produced, while inflation tracks how fast prices are rising. When demand outstrips supply, prices tend to climb, and central banks may respond by raising interest rates. If growth turns negative for two consecutive quarters, the economy is said to be in recession. Governments then try to stimulate demand through spending or tax cuts.', ['What is recession, according to the text?', 'Negative growth for two quarters', 'High growth', 'Rising exports'], ['Central banks lower rates when inflation rises.', 'False'], ['GDP was invented in 1934.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Describe a trend in an economy (inflation, prices or unemployment) in 8–10 sentences using verbs and adverbs of change.', 'rose|fell|sharply|due to', 70, 'In 2022 inflation rose sharply from 2% to 8% due to higher energy prices. The central bank responded by raising interest rates. As a result, demand fell slightly. Unemployment remained stable, but growth slowed down. Economists expect prices to stabilise next year.'],
      sp: ['Describe how prices have changed in your country recently.', 'Prices have risen steadily over the past year, mainly due to higher energy costs.'],
      ts: [['A fall in economic activity:', 'recession', 'inflation', 'revenue'], ['“Kamomad” in English:', 'deficit', 'revenue', 'budget'], ['Prices ___ sharply last month.', 'rose', 'raised', 'rised']] },
    { t: ['Entrepreneurship', 'Tadbirkorlik'],
      obj: ['Biznes g‘oyasini taqdim etasiz va tadbirkorlik xatarlari haqida gapirasiz.', 'You will pitch a business idea and talk about entrepreneurial risks.'],
      ex: ['Tadbirkorlik: start-up, entrepreneur, investor, capital, profit / loss, market niche (bozor oralig‘i), business plan, risk-taking, launch (ishga tushirmoq). Taqdimot iboralari: Our product is aimed at…, What makes us different is…, We expect to break even (zararsizlikka erishmoq) within two years.\nGerundiy va infinitiv: decide to, plan to, risk losing, avoid wasting. Uzoq muddat: by the end of next year we will have made a profit. Shart: unless, provided that, as long as.',  'Entrepreneurship: start-up, entrepreneur, investor, capital, profit / loss, market niche, business plan, risk-taking, launch. Pitching: Our product is aimed at…, What makes us different is…, We expect to break even within two years.\nGerund and infinitive: decide to, plan to, risk losing, avoid wasting. Future perfect: by the end of next year we will have made a profit. Condition: unless, provided that, as long as.'],
      eg: [['Our product is aimed at young professionals.', 'Mahsulotimiz yosh mutaxassislarga mo‘ljallangan.'], ['We expect to break even within two years.', 'Ikki yil ichida zararsizlikka erishishni kutyapmiz.'], ['She risked losing her savings.', 'U jamg‘armasini yo‘qotish xavfini o‘z zimmasiga oldi.'], ['By next year we will have made a profit.', 'Kelasi yilga kelib biz foyda ko‘rgan bo‘lamiz.']],
      w: [['entrepreneur', 'tadbirkor', 'предприниматель', 'noun', 'An entrepreneur starts new companies.', 'Tadbirkor yangi kompaniyalar ochadi.', 'ˌɒntrəprəˈnɜː'], ['start-up', 'yangi boshlangan kompaniya', 'стартап', 'noun', 'The start-up raised funds.', 'Start-ap mablag‘ jalb qildi.', 'ˈstɑːt ʌp'], ['investor', 'investor', 'инвестор', 'noun', 'Investors liked the idea.', 'Investorlarga g‘oya yoqdi.', 'ɪnˈvestə'], ['profit', 'foyda', 'прибыль', 'noun', 'The firm made a profit.', 'Firma foyda ko‘rdi.', 'ˈprɒfɪt'], ['launch', 'ishga tushirmoq', 'запускать', 'verb', 'They will launch the app in May.', 'Ular ilovani mayda ishga tushiradi.', 'lɔːntʃ'], ['niche', 'bozor oralig‘i', 'ниша', 'noun', 'They found a market niche.', 'Ular bozor oralig‘ini topdi.', 'niːʃ']],
      g: [['We expect ___ even within two years.', 'to break', 'breaking', 'break', 'expect to + fe’l.'], ['By next year we ___ a profit.', 'will have made', 'will make', 'are making', 'Future Perfect.']],
      dlg: ['Investor: What makes your start-up different? Founder: Our app is aimed at students and lets them find tutors in minutes. Investor: How do you plan to make a profit? Founder: Through commission. We expect to break even within two years. Investor: What are the risks? Founder: We risk losing customers if we fail to keep prices low.', 'How will the start-up make a profit?', 'Through commission', 'By selling phones', 'Through advertising only', 'The founder says “Through commission”.'],
      rd: ['Starting a business requires more than a good idea. Successful entrepreneurs identify a market niche, test their product on a small scale and prepare a business plan that shows how the company will earn money. Many start-ups fail within the first five years, usually because they run out of capital or misjudge demand. Nevertheless, those who learn from failure and adapt quickly are more likely to succeed, provided that they can attract investors or loyal customers.', ['Why do many start-ups fail?', 'They run out of capital or misjudge demand', 'They advertise too much', 'They have no ideas'], ['A good idea alone is enough to succeed.', 'False'], ['The writer owns a company.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a short business pitch (10–12 sentences) for a start-up idea: product, target customers, how it will earn money, risks.', 'aimed at|what makes us different|break even|will have', 80, 'Our start-up offers a mobile app that connects students with tutors. The product is aimed at university students. What makes us different is that tutors are verified. We plan to earn money through a small commission. We expect to break even within two years. The main risk is competition. By the end of next year we will have reached ten thousand users.'],
      sp: ['Pitch your business idea in 30 seconds.', 'Our product is aimed at students. What makes us different is that it is free for the first month.'],
      ts: [['A newly established company:', 'start-up', 'niche', 'deficit'], ['“Tadbirkor” in English:', 'entrepreneur', 'investor', 'profit'], ['We risk ___ money.', 'losing', 'to lose', 'lose']] },
    { t: ['Work–life balance', 'Ish va shaxsiy hayot muvozanati'],
      obj: ['Ish va shaxsiy hayot muvozanati haqida fikr bildirib, takliflar berasiz.', 'You will express opinions and make suggestions about work–life balance.'],
      ex: ['Muvozanat: burnout (kuyib ketish), long working hours, flexitime, paid leave, overwork, quality time, stress-related illness, productivity. Iboralar: strike a balance (muvozanat topmoq), cope with, juggle (bir necha ishni uddalamoq), switch off (o‘chirmoq/dam olmoq), take a break.\nQaror: wish / if only: I wish I had more free time. (hozirgi afsus). I wish I hadn’t worked so much. (o‘tgan afsus). Taklif: employers ought to…, it would be better if…, there should be a limit on…',  'Balance: burnout, long working hours, flexitime, paid leave, overwork, quality time, stress-related illness, productivity. Phrases: strike a balance, cope with, juggle, switch off, take a break.\nWishes: wish / if only: I wish I had more free time (present regret). I wish I hadn’t worked so much (past regret). Suggestions: employers ought to…, it would be better if…, there should be a limit on…'],
      eg: [['I wish I had more free time.', 'Kashki ko‘proq bo‘sh vaqtim bo‘lsa.'], ['I wish I hadn’t worked so much last year.', 'Kashki o‘tgan yili bunchalik ko‘p ishlamaganimda.'], ['It is hard to strike a balance between work and family.', 'Ish va oila o‘rtasida muvozanat topish qiyin.'], ['Employees need to switch off after work.', 'Xodimlar ishdan keyin “o‘chirilishi” kerak.']],
      w: [['burnout', 'kuyib ketish', 'выгорание', 'noun', 'Burnout is a serious risk.', 'Kuyib ketish jiddiy xavf.', 'ˈbɜːnaʊt'], ['flexitime', 'moslashuvchan ish vaqti', 'гибкий график', 'noun', 'Flexitime suits parents.', 'Moslashuvchan ish vaqti ota-onalarga mos.', 'ˈfleksitaɪm'], ['juggle', 'bir nechta ishni uddalamoq', 'совмещать', 'verb', 'She juggles work and study.', 'U ish va o‘qishni uddalaydi.', 'ˈdʒʌɡl'], ['switch off', 'dam olmoq (uzilmoq)', 'отключаться', 'phrasal verb', 'I cannot switch off at night.', 'Kechasi uzila olmayman.', 'swɪtʃ ɒf'], ['overwork', 'haddan ortiq ishlamoq', 'переутомление', 'noun', 'Overwork harms health.', 'Haddan ortiq ishlash sog‘liqqa zarar.', 'ˌəʊvəˈwɜːk'], ['leave', 'ta’til (ish joyida)', 'отпуск', 'noun', 'He took paid leave.', 'U haq to‘lanadigan ta’til oldi.', 'liːv']],
      g: [['I wish I ___ more free time.', 'had', 'have', 'would have', 'Hozirgi afsus — wish + Past Simple.'], ['I wish I ___ so much last year.', 'hadn’t worked', 'didn’t work', 'wouldn’t work', 'O‘tgan afsus — wish + Past Perfect.']],
      dlg: ['Manager: You seem exhausted. Anna: I wish I had more time for my family. I am juggling too many projects. Manager: Burnout is a real risk. It would be better if you took a few days of paid leave. Anna: I can’t switch off when I am at home. Manager: Then let’s try flexitime.', 'What does the manager suggest?', 'Paid leave and flexitime', 'More projects', 'Working at night', 'He suggests paid leave and flexitime.'],
      rd: ['Long working hours are often seen as a sign of commitment, but research shows that they can reduce productivity and damage health. People who work more than fifty-five hours a week face a higher risk of stress-related illness and burnout. Some countries have responded by introducing a legal limit on the working week, while many companies now offer flexitime and the right to disconnect after hours. Experts conclude that rest is not a luxury; it is a condition for good performance.', ['What do experts conclude?', 'Rest is a condition for good performance', 'Rest is a luxury', 'Long hours are always best'], ['Working very long hours improves health.', 'False'], ['Everyone in Europe works 35 hours.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write an opinion text (10–12 sentences) on how employers and employees can improve work–life balance; include two wish sentences.', 'i wish|it would be better if|burnout|flexitime', 80, 'It is difficult to strike a balance between work and personal life. I wish I had more free time for my family. Long working hours can lead to burnout. It would be better if employers offered flexitime. Employees should also learn to switch off after work. Overall, rest is a condition for good performance.'],
      sp: ['Say what you would change in your daily routine to have better balance.', 'I wish I had more free time. I would spend less time on my phone and more time with my family.'],
      ts: [['Complete exhaustion from work:', 'burnout', 'flexitime', 'leave'], ['“Uzilmoq, dam olmoq” (phrasal):', 'switch off', 'cope up', 'give in'], ['I wish I ___ more time. (now)', 'had', 'have', 'would have']] },
    { t: ['Reading economic texts', 'Iqtisodiy matnlarni o‘qish'],
      obj: ['Iqtisodiy matnlarni o‘qiyotganda asosiy fikr, dalil va xulosani ajratib olasiz.', 'You will identify main ideas, evidence and conclusions when reading economic texts.'],
      ex: ['O‘qish strategiyalari: skimming (umumiy ko‘z yugurtirish), scanning (kerakli ma’lumotni izlash), topic sentence (mavzu gap), inference (xulosa chiqarish), author’s purpose. Matn signallari: however (qarama-qarshilik), therefore (natija), for instance (misol), in other words (boshqacha aytganda).\nGrafik tavsifi: percentages, double, triple, a fall of 20 per cent, accounts for (… ni tashkil qiladi). Raqamlarni o‘qish: 2.5 per cent — two point five per cent. IELTS uslubidagi savollar: True/False/Not Given, matching headings.', 'Reading strategies: skimming, scanning, topic sentence, inference, author’s purpose. Signals: however (contrast), therefore (result), for instance (example), in other words (restatement).\nChart language: percentages, double, triple, a fall of 20 per cent, accounts for. Reading numbers: 2.5 per cent — two point five per cent. IELTS-style questions: True/False/Not Given, matching headings.'],
      eg: [['Skim the text first, then scan for numbers.', 'Avval matnga ko‘z yugurtiring, keyin raqamlarni izlang.'], ['Services account for 60 per cent of GDP.', 'Xizmatlar YaIMning 60 foizini tashkil qiladi.'], ['In other words, prices doubled in a decade.', 'Boshqacha aytganda, narxlar o‘n yilda ikki baravar oshdi.'], ['The author’s purpose is to warn readers about inflation.', 'Muallifning maqsadi — o‘quvchilarni inflyatsiyadan ogohlantirish.']],
      w: [['skim', 'ko‘z yugurtirib chiqmoq', 'бегло просматривать', 'verb', 'Skim the article quickly.', 'Maqolaga tez ko‘z yugurtiring.', 'skɪm'], ['scan', 'kerakli ma’lumotni izlamoq', 'искать информацию', 'verb', 'Scan the table for dates.', 'Jadvaldan sanalarni izlang.', 'skæn'], ['infer', 'xulosa chiqarmoq', 'делать вывод', 'verb', 'We can infer the writer’s opinion.', 'Muallif fikrini xulosa qilamiz.', 'ɪnˈfɜː'], ['account for', 'tashkil qilmoq', 'составлять', 'phrasal verb', 'Exports account for half of income.', 'Eksport daromadning yarmini tashkil qiladi.', 'əˈkaʊnt fɔː'], ['double', 'ikki baravar oshmoq', 'удваиваться', 'verb', 'Prices doubled in ten years.', 'Narxlar o‘n yilda ikki baravar oshdi.', 'ˈdʌbl'], ['purpose', 'maqsad', 'цель', 'noun', 'What is the writer’s purpose?', 'Muallifning maqsadi nima?', 'ˈpɜːpəs']],
      g: [['Services ___ for 60 per cent of GDP.', 'account', 'count', 'accounts to', 'account for — tashkil qilmoq.'], ['Prices ___ in a decade. (x2)', 'doubled', 'double', 'doubles', 'O‘tgan zamon.']],
      dlg: ['Tutor: How do you approach a long economic text? Student: First I skim it to get the main idea. Tutor: And for a question about a number? Student: I scan for the figure and then read around it. Tutor: Good. Watch signal words such as however and therefore. They show how ideas are connected.', 'Why should you notice signal words?', 'They show how ideas are connected', 'They are always wrong', 'They give numbers', 'The tutor says “They show how ideas are connected”.'],
      rd: ['Over the past thirty years, the share of services in the economy has grown steadily, while agriculture has declined. In 1990 services accounted for 45 per cent of national output; by 2020 the figure had risen to 62 per cent. The authors suggest that this shift is linked to rising incomes: as people become wealthier, they spend more on education, health and entertainment rather than basic goods. However, they warn that service jobs are not equally distributed across regions.', ['What did services account for in 2020?', '62 per cent', '45 per cent', '30 per cent'], ['Agriculture has increased its share.', 'False'], ['Services employ more women than men.', 'Not Given']],
      wr: ['Write a summary (8–10 sentences) of a short economic text, covering the main idea, two pieces of evidence and the conclusion.', 'the text|accounts for|however|therefore', 70, 'The text explains how the economy has changed over thirty years. It shows that services now account for 62 per cent of output, compared with 45 per cent in 1990. In other words, services have become dominant. However, the authors warn that service jobs are not distributed equally. Therefore, governments should support less developed regions.'],
      sp: ['Summarise the main idea of an article you have read recently in three sentences.', 'The article explains that services now dominate the economy. However, jobs are unequal across regions. Therefore, support is needed.'],
      ts: [['Reading quickly for the general idea:', 'skimming', 'scanning', 'inferring'], ['“Maqsad” in English:', 'purpose', 'figure', 'share'], ['Exports ___ for half of GDP.', 'account', 'make up to', 'count']] },
  ], exam: [['I wish I ___ more money right now.', 'had', 'have', 'would have', 'grammar'], ['By 2030 the company ___ its goals.', 'will have achieved', 'will achieving', 'achieved', 'grammar'], ['A general rise in prices:', 'inflation', 'deficit', 'revenue', 'vocabulary']] },
];
